    "body": "@achristensen07 do you have thoughts on this? It seems WebKit might have inconsistent handling of `javascript:` URLs. E.g., on https://jsdom.github.io/whatwg-url/ `javascript://test:test` does not throw, but in `new URL()` it does. Contrast that with `test://test:test`.\r\n\r\n@ricea I could see us making a distinct decision there (e.g., modifying \"cannot have a username/password/port\" to include the \"`javascript`\" scheme), so that's probably fair. But I think we need something stronger than \"uncomfortable\", especially if the parser does still allow for them to be included.",
