    "created_at": "2023-03-07T15:40:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-07T15:40:52Z",
    "body": "Yeah, Chromium had a lot of javascript URL parsing changes a couple of years ago. I believe that is now fully aligned with the HTML spec, but of course the URL parser itself is not aligned yet.\r\n\r\nI think failing to parse in the URL parser is the best idea. Unfortunately, the non-special URL parsing in Chrome still doesn't actually parse apart authority and path.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why WebKit behaves differently between `new URL()` and `<a href>` though – I presume the latter uses a different parser for `javascript:` URLs?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
